        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Blight"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "(aura, necromancy, poison, primal)\n\n30 feet. A plant entering or starting its turn in the corpseroot's aura begins to wither and must succeed at a DC 27 Fortitude save or become sickened 2 (sickened 4 on a critical failure). A plant that succeeds is temporarily immune for 1 minute.\n\nA plant that stays in the aura for 7 consecutive days must succeed at a DC 27 Fortitude save or die. If the plant was a creature or tree, it rises as a corpseroot. The newly risen corpseroot can't create more corpseroots but has all other corpseroot abilities. Plants that are neither magical nor creatures automatically fail saves against blight."
            },
            "id": "b017519a-22c9-497a-98a0-bba6cf76a438",
            "updated_at": {
              "value": "2026-03-17T12:41:28.527612"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "resource_id": "monster_trait",
          "stats": {
            "trait_name": {
              "value": "Plant"
            },
            "trait_description": {
              "value": "When it isn't in danger, the corpseroot spends 1 minute rooting to the earth, becoming planted in place. While the corpseroot is planted and immobile, creatures must actively Seek and succeed at a DC 36 Perception check (DC 40 in forests) to detect the corpseroot's true nature."
            },
            "id": "f4c8c7ca-1ebb-4e81-9a40-c806014af652",
